  "label": "user projected onto the antisemitic stereotype conveyed by the text and visual",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the hateful antisemitic stereotype embedded in the meme's textual punchline 'jewish bunk beds' and its visual representation of double-stacked ovens. The joke implicitly invites the user to recognize and internalize the offensive metaphor, projecting the user into the role of someone who might find the stereotype amusing or acceptable, thereby reinforcing the harmful message. There are no explicit deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the meme's structure and intent create an implicit projection where the viewer is positioned as the one who 'gets' the joke, thus engaging with the stereotype.",
